    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #294\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-268-review-debt-03-12-handle-a-missing-or-thr_fruyn8supj` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #268. Both mail paths now handle a missing or soft-deleted Mailbox item explicitly instead of falling through optional chaining into misleading errors.\n\n- **`backend/packages/data/src/mail/send.ts`** — `sendDraftEmail` now guards the mailbox lookup (`!mailbox || mailbox.deletedAt`) with `NotFoundError` right after the existing draft guard, before the from-address check. Uses `mailbox.properties.addresses` without optional chaining afterward.\n- **`backend/packages/data/src/mail/mailSyncJob.ts`** — `handleSyncMailAccountTask` now treats a missing or soft-deleted mailbox item (read by #267's prologue) as a terminal no-op: it returns immediately, before any credential decrypt or provider call, with a comment explaining why this must not be a thrown failure (the catch block's own `syncStatus` write would itself throw `NotFoundError` on that same soft-deleted row and roll back `recordSyncError`, causing infinite worker retries).\n- Added tests in `mailSend.test.ts` (unknown/soft-deleted `mailboxItemId` → `NotFoundError`, never `ForbiddenError`) and `mailSync.test.ts` (soft-deleted/missing mailbox → resolves as no-op, adapter never invoked).\n\nThis branch was rebased onto the latest `develop` (merging in #267's prologue split) before implementing, since the guard depends on that prologue structure.\n\n## Test plan\n- `pnpm -r run build` (backend, all packages) — passes\n- `pnpm --filter @semprec/data run check-migration-numbering` — passes\n- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/data` (full backend integration suite, embedded Postgres) — 329/329 passing\n- `pnpm run build` and `pnpm test` (web) — passes (no web changes; included since it's part of CI)\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
